            <ArticleTitle>[Epileptic headaches (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author describes three observations characterized by the following similar features: 1. Children, between 2 and 9 years, suffering from attacks of sterotyped headaches. 2. EEG with bursts of high- voltage paroxysmal discharges, mainly during hyperventilation. 3. Efficiency of antiepileptic drugs contrary to antimigrainous treatment. These headaches are considered by the author as &quot;epileptic&quot;, and this diagnosis is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
